# Target C: first-third certificate for the final order-1 `(3,2,2,1)` support class

Date: 2026-09-25

Status: exact finite partial closure of representatives `0..107` of the 324 fixed-support cycle-set representatives for

```text
{1234,1235,1456,2467}
```

in the eight-no-root `k=5,D=-1,d_root=1,p=3,m=4,(3,2,2,1)` branch, conditional on the structural reductions already proved in the repository. This is one third of the final stabilizer-order-1 support class. It does not close the remaining representatives `108..323`, the full `p=3` branch, Target C-II, or Erdos Problem #99.

## Global support data

The support stabilizer is trivial. Hence there are 324 fixed-support cycle-set representatives and `5040*324 = 1632960` labeled cycle sets in the whole class.

Every representative touches 15 root blocks. The complete touched-root family has exact rank 11 and nullity 4. Exactly 232 choices of three singleton blocks leave the remaining complete-root family with nullity one.

## Executed finite census

The first 108 representatives were split into six independent 18-representative subshards:

```text
[0,18):    4176  112752   84888  4104  {0:4104}  maxnorm^2=36
[18,36):   4176  112752   84888  4104  {0:4104}  maxnorm^2=36
[36,54):   4176  112752   86940  4644  {0:4644}  maxnorm^2=36
[54,72):   4176  112752   86940  4644  {0:4644}  maxnorm^2=36
[72,90):   4176  112752   86940  4644  {0:4644}  maxnorm^2=36
[90,108):  4176  112752   84888  3672  {0:3672}  maxnorm^2=36
```

The numeric columns are admissible singleton triples, singleton-direction states, coefficient-rank-three states, generalized-weight-admissible states, and the external relation-rank increment census.

Aggregate over representatives `0..107`:

```text
admissible singleton triples       25056
singleton-direction states        676512
coefficient-rank-three states     515484
generalized-weight states          25812
external increment census      {0:25812}
```

All 25,812 generalized-weight-admissible states have external relation-rank increment zero. The established branch reduction requires increment five. Therefore no survivor occurs among representatives `0..107`.

Ranks are computed modulo `P=2^127-1`. Lucas-Lehmer passes. The maximum squared relation-row norm in these subshards is 36, and `P^2 > 36^15`, so the repository's Hadamard argument certifies the modular rank results over `Q`.

The six subshards were executed locally with the current-main coordinate formulas. The companion verifier stores the hard expected census and re-enumerates the support metadata. Its `--subshard 0` path was also executed after construction; all six census rows above come from executed runs of the equivalent enumeration logic.

## Remaining bottleneck

For this support class, representatives `108..323` remain unchecked by this certificate.

Across existing certificate branches, the other first order-1 support class `{1234,1235,1246,1367}` is already closed, and the final order-2 class `{1234,1235,1267,1467}` also has a certificate, but neither result is assumed to be on authoritative `main` here.

The other unresolved `k=5` arithmetic branches remain `D=-2,(d_root,p)=(0,5)` and `D=-1,(d_root,p)=(0,6)`.
